      "content": "that makes sense, but honestly some of the older residents are being way too stubborn about it. they're basically just trying to keep the neighborhood exclusive and keep property values high at the expense of everyone else. is it okay to basically tell them that their 'neighborhood character' arguments are just a cover for NIMBYism and that the city needs to prioritize progress over their personal preferences?",
